WEBVTT

00:07.500 --> 00:10.010
One, two, one, two...

00:10.400 --> 00:12.960
One, two, one, two...

00:13.410 --> 00:15.950
One, two, one, two...

00:16.200 --> 00:18.410
One, two, one, two...

00:18.800 --> 00:21.230
Ready, halt!

00:24.470 --> 00:27.650
This reminds me of something...

00:28.090 --> 00:31.920
It's no fun marching by myself, though.

00:44.900 --> 00:46.150
Yum!

00:46.150 --> 00:47.940
Yum!

00:47.940 --> 00:49.150
Yum! Yum!

00:49.150 --> 00:51.440
Yummy!

02:22.030 --> 02:25.200
Fried Mandarins

02:22.030 --> 02:25.200
40kcal each

02:22.810 --> 02:25.200
So these are fried mandarins.

02:25.420 --> 02:26.380
Yup.

02:26.080 --> 02:30.120
17: "Mandarins! Mandarins! Fried mandarins?"

02:26.680 --> 02:28.780
I've heard they're good for your health.

02:28.780 --> 02:31.380
How are they different
from ordinary mandarins?

02:32.930 --> 02:34.500
Peel and all?

02:34.870 --> 02:37.030
It's healthier that way.

02:37.030 --> 02:39.770
It'll fix your cold in a jiffy.

02:40.830 --> 02:42.870
Fried mandarins, huh?

02:42.870 --> 02:45.600
It appears to be popular in some regions.

02:45.940 --> 02:49.930
Frying it boosts the nutritional
value of the peel.

02:49.930 --> 02:54.330
It's a great way to
get yourself back in health.

02:54.330 --> 02:58.540
You could say it's one of
your grandma's old-timey tricks.

02:58.840 --> 03:00.990
I see...

03:01.590 --> 03:03.780
It's Chopin-san. What does he want?

03:03.780 --> 03:05.910
From: Chopin-san

03:03.990 --> 03:05.910
Kanae's down.
Dying!

03:07.410 --> 03:09.000
Kanae!

03:09.390 --> 03:10.910
Are you all right?

03:10.910 --> 03:12.540
Kanae! Hang in there!

03:13.690 --> 03:15.630
Sousuke?

03:15.630 --> 03:17.300
Yeah, it's me!

03:20.010 --> 03:21.660
Don't die, Kanae!

03:21.660 --> 03:23.510
Don't die!

03:22.290 --> 03:23.510
Damn it, shut up!

03:24.210 --> 03:26.310
Are you all right, my kitten?

03:26.310 --> 03:27.390
Yes.

03:28.580 --> 03:30.520
Take it easy.

03:30.520 --> 03:32.140
I'm sorry.

03:32.140 --> 03:34.480
The flu is pretty rough this year.

03:35.980 --> 03:36.690
Flu?

03:36.690 --> 03:37.940
Yeah.

03:37.940 --> 03:40.620
That's why I told you to keep quiet.

03:40.620 --> 03:43.000
Jeez, I freaked out.

03:43.000 --> 03:45.660
Chopin-san texted me, saying she's dying.

03:45.660 --> 03:47.470
We're the ones dying.

03:48.080 --> 03:49.470
Exactly.

03:49.470 --> 03:52.900
Who's going to make our meals
with Kanae out?

03:52.900 --> 03:55.410
Someone has to do the laundry
and clean our rooms, too.

03:55.410 --> 03:56.640
Please, everyone,

03:56.640 --> 03:59.740
you should be worried for my little
kitten, not for yourselves.

04:00.610 --> 04:03.050
We need her to recover soon.

04:03.320 --> 04:06.660
If only there were a medicine that
could cure the flu instantly.

04:06.660 --> 04:08.720
How could there be such a...

04:10.900 --> 04:12.480
There is! Fried mandarins!

04:12.970 --> 04:14.350
Fried mandarins?

04:14.350 --> 04:16.600
What, never heard of it?

04:16.600 --> 04:18.770
It's popular in the countryside.

04:18.770 --> 04:21.920
The peel goes, like, bam! Woosh!

04:21.920 --> 04:23.430
It just becomes super awesome,

04:23.430 --> 04:25.480
and it cures your flu, like, instantly.

04:25.480 --> 04:28.840
It's, like, old-timey wisdom, or something.

04:28.840 --> 04:30.910
I never thought you'd be
so knowledgeable, tool.

04:30.910 --> 04:33.300
He's just parroting what I told him.

04:33.300 --> 04:34.920
And not even very accurately.

04:35.250 --> 04:36.170
That's weak.

04:36.420 --> 04:40.160
But if it works for the flu,
perhaps it's worth trying.

04:40.160 --> 04:42.940
I know where to get some
really good mandarins.

04:43.240 --> 04:44.370
I'll go get them.

04:50.520 --> 04:54.060
This is totally going to fix Kanae's flu.

04:54.060 --> 04:55.350
And then...

04:56.460 --> 04:59.250
It's thanks to you that my flu went away!

04:59.250 --> 05:01.320
Thanks so much!

05:13.010 --> 05:15.410
Now, don't be shy!

05:16.020 --> 05:18.500
Eat the whole thing, peel and all!

05:25.160 --> 05:26.430
It's good.

05:26.650 --> 05:28.000
Yay!

05:28.350 --> 05:29.140
What's it taste like?

05:29.400 --> 05:33.090
It's a gentle taste, like sweet potato.

05:33.090 --> 05:35.920
It's like it's warming me up from the inside.

05:35.920 --> 05:37.950
Guess it's good to try, then.

05:39.100 --> 05:40.880
You were testing it on me?

05:40.880 --> 05:43.370
Hey, it was good, right?

05:44.230 --> 05:45.730
Tasty.

05:46.030 --> 05:47.240
It's savory.

05:47.240 --> 05:50.230
A harmony of wisdom, innovation, and love.

05:50.230 --> 05:52.160
You're absolutely right, Senpai.

05:53.390 --> 05:54.790
Aren't you having any, Motes-san?

05:55.170 --> 05:58.760
Nope. I ate a bunch earlier, so I'm all full.

05:59.060 --> 06:00.750
I'll have them fried some other time.

06:01.170 --> 06:05.300
Don't be so finicky, Cho-chan.
You can eat the peel, too.

06:08.000 --> 06:10.800
What's the point of frying it, then?

06:29.700 --> 06:31.660
On Duty

06:36.950 --> 06:38.460
No way, obviously.

06:38.460 --> 06:39.700
Knock it off!

06:39.700 --> 06:40.460
Thank you for—

07:05.400 --> 07:07.190
Somebody!

07:08.010 --> 07:08.860
What happened?

07:09.140 --> 07:10.190
Senpai...

07:10.560 --> 07:12.640
Stay strong! Senpai!

07:13.960 --> 07:15.110
Beethes-san?

07:15.110 --> 07:18.850
By the time I saw him, he was
already on the floor, in pain.

07:19.310 --> 07:19.960
He's hot.

07:20.570 --> 07:22.860
Bring him something to cool him off.

07:24.610 --> 07:26.060
Let's carry him.

07:26.060 --> 07:26.860
Right!

07:30.000 --> 07:31.350
What's wrong, Schu-san?

07:31.650 --> 07:34.190
I'm feeling dizzy...

07:54.810 --> 07:57.580
Not just Beethoven, but Schubert, too?

07:57.580 --> 08:00.480
He didn't have to take it
<i>that</i> far with his imitating.

08:00.480 --> 08:03.470
I wonder if they both caught Kanae's flu.

08:03.470 --> 08:04.500
No.

08:05.180 --> 08:07.340
That's not the flu.

08:07.340 --> 08:09.000
Then what?

08:10.140 --> 08:11.010
A curse.

08:11.620 --> 08:12.630
A curse?

08:13.170 --> 08:13.890
Yeah.

08:21.270 --> 08:23.190
This is a curse.

08:24.020 --> 08:24.900
A curse?

08:25.390 --> 08:29.040
Hasshie planted the seed
in the yard that became

08:29.040 --> 08:31.090
the mandarin tree that he's been tending to.

08:31.090 --> 08:34.510
The tree is angry, because we
took it without his consent.

08:34.510 --> 08:37.460
This is a result of that curse.

08:38.300 --> 08:40.220
You can understand what Hasshie says?!

08:40.220 --> 08:41.780
We don't seem to have any choice
but to believe him.

08:41.780 --> 08:42.750
Just like that?

08:43.500 --> 08:44.330
Look.

08:51.020 --> 08:52.920
This color... Isn't it obvious?

08:53.440 --> 08:54.930
The curse of the mandarins.

08:56.150 --> 08:57.890
It's your fault.

08:58.840 --> 09:01.090
If what he said is true,

09:01.090 --> 09:04.490
you caused this by picking the mandarins.

09:04.490 --> 09:07.800
I just wanted to make Kanae happy.

09:07.800 --> 09:10.570
Besides, I haven't been cursed,
even though I picked them.

09:10.570 --> 09:12.200
Arguing aside,

09:12.200 --> 09:15.460
shouldn't you think about
what to do about those two?

09:15.460 --> 09:16.280
You're right.

09:16.540 --> 09:17.780
I have an idea.

09:17.780 --> 09:18.730
That was quick!

09:18.730 --> 09:20.270
It's a curse, right?

09:20.270 --> 09:22.580
Then there's only one way to deal with it.

09:23.840 --> 09:25.040
Amen!

09:25.860 --> 09:27.050
An exorcism?

09:27.050 --> 09:28.680
Why am I part of this?

09:32.550 --> 09:33.670
You, too.

09:33.670 --> 09:37.010
A E I O U! A E I O U!

09:39.950 --> 09:41.180
How about this, then?

09:41.540 --> 09:43.130
Evil be gone! Evil be gone!

09:43.130 --> 09:45.830
Evil be gone!

09:44.090 --> 09:47.070
I'm pretty sure Motes-san's
getting it fundamentally wrong...

09:46.710 --> 09:49.150
Come on, put your heart into it!

09:49.150 --> 09:50.350
Why am I doing this?

09:52.660 --> 09:53.610
What's this?

09:54.490 --> 09:55.930
A stem, it looks like.

09:55.930 --> 09:56.530
A stem?

09:57.070 --> 10:00.860
Like what's on fruits and vegetables?

10:01.160 --> 10:02.700
Curse of the mandarins...

10:02.700 --> 10:04.440
Dude, this is legit.

10:04.440 --> 10:06.370
We have to help them quick.

10:07.150 --> 10:08.210
All right...

10:12.330 --> 10:13.120
There.

10:13.120 --> 10:14.960
What's with the scribbles?

10:15.430 --> 10:18.130
They're not scribbles. They're sutras.

10:18.130 --> 10:23.200
There are folktales where people banish
evil spirits by writing sutras on themselves.

10:23.200 --> 10:24.720
I believe it's worth a shot.

10:25.040 --> 10:26.170
Huh.

10:26.170 --> 10:28.590
I guess it's better than nothing.

10:29.090 --> 10:32.100
We're going to have to see how it goes.

10:32.980 --> 10:34.730
My head's suddenly...

10:34.730 --> 10:36.400
Not you, too!

10:36.900 --> 10:38.950
I'm going to go lie down in my room.

10:40.290 --> 10:41.950
Keep an eye on those two.

10:41.950 --> 10:43.300
Okay.

10:47.740 --> 10:51.640
Man, will these scribbles actually work?

10:52.770 --> 10:54.530
Let's <i>really</i> draw.

10:56.200 --> 11:00.630
Gotta cheer things up when you're down.

11:00.630 --> 11:02.050
Senpai...

11:02.050 --> 11:03.930
This is our fate.

11:05.260 --> 11:06.540
Please, stop.

11:06.540 --> 11:08.550
You can't say that with that face.

11:08.930 --> 11:10.220
I know.

11:17.050 --> 11:19.660
I laughed too much. Now I'm thirsty.

11:49.050 --> 11:49.870
What?

11:50.170 --> 11:53.190
B-Beethes-san and Schu-san...

11:59.820 --> 12:01.840
The curse is speeding up.

12:01.840 --> 12:04.320
Hey, we're out of juice.

12:04.940 --> 12:06.350
Can someone go out to buy some?

12:06.350 --> 12:08.330
Now's not the time!

12:08.760 --> 12:10.110
Look, huge mandarins!

12:10.110 --> 12:12.180
D-Don't go near them!

12:12.180 --> 12:15.270
The faces I drew fit them perfectly.

12:15.270 --> 12:17.040
You drew those, Motes-san?

12:17.040 --> 12:17.800
Yup.

12:18.690 --> 12:20.550
Why did you do that?

12:20.780 --> 12:23.190
Hey, let's try peeling them.

12:23.680 --> 12:24.700
No! No!

12:24.700 --> 12:27.760
What if you make it even worse?

12:42.370 --> 12:43.070
What the heck?

12:59.380 --> 13:00.360
Hullo.

13:03.650 --> 13:05.340
Hullo again.

13:07.010 --> 13:09.010
M-M-Motes-san!

13:15.670 --> 13:18.230
This is getting fun.

13:18.230 --> 13:19.230
Count me in!

13:22.060 --> 13:24.160
How can you be enjoying this?

13:26.600 --> 13:27.600
Liszt-san!

13:27.600 --> 13:29.410
Beethes-san and Schu-san...

13:35.730 --> 13:36.920
Love.

13:38.350 --> 13:40.180
Fate.

13:39.850 --> 13:41.750
M-Motes-san...

13:40.500 --> 13:41.750
Senpai.

13:45.980 --> 13:47.130
Bye-bye!

13:47.920 --> 13:48.840
You're bailing?

13:49.270 --> 13:51.320
No, we're playing tag!

14:01.460 --> 14:02.860
Good luck!

14:02.860 --> 14:05.320
Don't leave me!

14:05.760 --> 14:07.610
Love!

14:07.860 --> 14:09.620
Fate.

14:10.250 --> 14:11.870
Senpai.

14:13.410 --> 14:14.580
Stay away!

14:14.880 --> 14:15.700
No!

14:23.870 --> 14:25.300
Chopin-san!

14:25.300 --> 14:28.160
You saved me because
you thought I'd be useful, right?

14:28.160 --> 14:29.800
Trust you to make the right choice.

14:30.110 --> 14:32.210
I just don't trust people.

14:32.210 --> 14:33.810
Oh. I see.

14:48.750 --> 14:50.690
The drumming...

14:51.510 --> 14:52.580
Sousuke...

14:52.880 --> 14:55.080
You were the one who abandoned him.

15:00.800 --> 15:03.250
Huh? They aren't coming after me at all.

15:03.500 --> 15:04.590
Jeez.

15:05.440 --> 15:07.630
Hey, you got away too, huh?

15:07.630 --> 15:08.840
Wow.

15:10.070 --> 15:10.850
Later.

15:15.030 --> 15:15.920
What?

15:15.920 --> 15:17.590
You ought to take responsibility.

15:18.590 --> 15:20.270
For the curse of the mandarins.

15:24.710 --> 15:26.140
Give me a second.

15:27.370 --> 15:28.500
This sound...

15:28.860 --> 15:31.160
It sounds really familiar.

15:31.680 --> 15:34.330
It was like that this morning, too.

15:35.830 --> 15:37.470
No, now's not the time.

15:37.470 --> 15:38.620
I know.

15:38.620 --> 15:40.800
Why don't you do something about it?

15:40.800 --> 15:42.330
Take care of it with your Musik.

15:42.330 --> 15:44.190
The curse is your fault.

15:44.190 --> 15:47.550
I guess, maybe, but...

15:47.550 --> 15:49.300
Take responsibility.

15:49.470 --> 15:50.340
Fate.

15:50.510 --> 15:51.380
Senpai.

15:51.550 --> 15:52.550
Love.

15:54.060 --> 15:55.650
All right, fine.

15:57.550 --> 15:59.850
We're done playing tag.

16:04.300 --> 16:05.190
Take that!

16:05.630 --> 16:07.330
Y-You did it.

16:20.460 --> 16:22.010
Wait, that's sweet.

16:22.010 --> 16:24.640
Is this orange juice?

16:24.640 --> 16:25.620
What?

16:25.620 --> 16:26.790
Give me some, too.

16:29.860 --> 16:31.630
It's yummy!

16:32.090 --> 16:34.100
Wh-What are you doing?

16:34.100 --> 16:35.930
Just one more sip!

16:36.820 --> 16:38.930
You don't care to own up, do you?

16:39.860 --> 16:41.640
The curse is your fault.

16:42.660 --> 16:45.090
What the hell are you thinking?

16:45.090 --> 16:47.590
I'm happy I got to have so much juice.

16:48.730 --> 16:49.980
Fine.

16:49.980 --> 16:52.080
Just stay put. Don't do anything.

16:53.150 --> 16:53.780
Wait.

17:07.570 --> 17:08.210
Wait.

17:12.700 --> 17:13.510
All right.

17:14.950 --> 17:18.220
I just thought up a good way
to stop the curse.

17:18.570 --> 17:21.180
Could you go lure them out for me?

17:24.380 --> 17:28.090
Olly olly oxen free!

17:29.000 --> 17:32.700
Olly olly oxen free!

17:40.950 --> 17:43.450
No one said they'd be so fast!

17:47.290 --> 17:48.750
Hurry!

17:49.600 --> 17:50.820
Okay.

17:50.820 --> 17:53.010
Lud-kun's flamethrower!

17:55.630 --> 17:59.640
If they're not going to go back to normal,
I'll make them into fried mandarins.

17:59.950 --> 18:03.600
Hang on a second!
They might still go back to normal!

18:03.890 --> 18:05.070
Look out.

18:05.370 --> 18:06.310
Move.

18:14.900 --> 18:16.130
Ow...

18:16.130 --> 18:18.160
Looks like it was jammed.

18:18.480 --> 18:21.770
There really is a fine line
between genius and insanity.

18:21.770 --> 18:23.040
Disaster.

18:23.840 --> 18:26.010
Fate.

18:26.010 --> 18:27.940
Senpai.

18:27.940 --> 18:29.380
Love.

18:29.380 --> 18:32.130
Oh, come on. Don't be so angry.

18:50.010 --> 18:51.940
I remember now!

18:53.800 --> 18:58.670
Fühle meine Musik!

19:06.890 --> 19:10.050
Forward march!

19:17.800 --> 19:19.030
Musik...

19:19.030 --> 19:21.440
Piano Sonata No. 11, third movement,

19:21.440 --> 19:23.130
the "Turkish March."

19:23.130 --> 19:28.240
Mozart is said to have written this piece
inspired by a Turkish marching band.

19:38.440 --> 19:41.660
Your lips are a forbidden fruit.

19:42.380 --> 19:45.240
I must have a taste.

19:46.690 --> 19:50.320
My passion for you is burning hot.

19:50.320 --> 19:52.460
Meltingly sweet...

19:52.830 --> 19:55.500
Yes, just like...

19:55.500 --> 19:57.660
A fried mandarin.

20:24.510 --> 20:26.730
Stop! I don't want to become a mandarin!

20:26.730 --> 20:28.890
I'm a machine!

20:28.830 --> 20:30.450
Man, that was fun.

20:29.380 --> 20:33.640
I'm not fit to become a mandarin!

20:30.450 --> 20:32.540
That was it?

20:32.880 --> 20:33.640
Yeah.

20:33.640 --> 20:36.540
I know what I was trying to remember now.
I feel all better.

20:34.090 --> 20:35.870
I'll short out!

20:36.810 --> 20:39.170
I won't even be a

20:37.500 --> 20:41.450
You haven't solved the bigger problem.

20:39.170 --> 20:41.910
rotten mandarin or anything!

20:41.450 --> 20:42.050
Huh?

20:41.920 --> 20:43.160
Please, stop!

20:43.160 --> 20:44.980
Stop!

20:44.980 --> 20:46.140
I'm a machine!

20:49.570 --> 20:51.520
You don't remember any of it?

20:51.520 --> 20:52.510
Nope.

20:52.920 --> 20:56.770
You scared the wits out of us, you know.

20:57.010 --> 20:58.570
I don't know what to say.

20:58.820 --> 21:00.690
I don't have any memory of last night.

21:01.030 --> 21:01.780
None.

21:01.780 --> 21:05.220
Hey, where does that leave me?
You guys attacked me!

21:06.900 --> 21:09.370
You're kind of glowing.

21:09.370 --> 21:11.080
I know!

21:11.080 --> 21:14.460
When I woke up,
my skin was all soft and squishy.

21:14.730 --> 21:16.710
I feel great, too.

21:16.710 --> 21:19.710
It's like my whole body was replaced.

21:20.080 --> 21:22.900
It seems that last night's
symptoms were not a curse,

21:22.900 --> 21:25.350
but rather some kind of metabolic change.

21:26.260 --> 21:30.410
It only happened to the ClassicaLoids
that ate fried mandarins.

21:30.410 --> 21:32.990
Which means the nutrients
in fried mandarin skin

21:32.990 --> 21:35.530
have a profound effect on
the ClassicaLoid body.

21:35.530 --> 21:38.710
It can be hypothesized
that yesterday's symptoms

21:38.710 --> 21:41.180
were part of a detoxification process.

21:41.180 --> 21:42.740
Yeah, way over my head.

21:42.740 --> 21:44.020
Morning.

21:44.020 --> 21:45.460
Sorry about last night.

21:45.460 --> 21:47.280
Hey, did you get over your flu?

21:47.500 --> 21:48.390
Yes.

21:48.390 --> 21:50.850
All better, thanks to the fried mandarin.

21:54.790 --> 21:56.350
What the hell happened?!

21:56.350 --> 21:57.760
Beethes!

21:57.760 --> 21:59.830
That wasn't me. It was Wolf.

22:00.170 --> 22:01.250
Where's Motes?!

22:01.560 --> 22:03.190
From what Cho-chan told me,

22:03.190 --> 22:05.850
he really made a mess last night.

22:05.850 --> 22:08.250
He might be in his room, reflecting.

22:08.250 --> 22:10.280
Who, him?

22:09.770 --> 22:11.500
Hey, guys.

22:11.500 --> 22:12.260
See?

22:15.370 --> 22:17.520
Huh? What's wrong, guys?

22:17.840 --> 22:19.920
Is there something on my face?

22:30.990 --> 22:33.990
To be continued

24:03.960 --> 24:25.690
MitsuruLoid and Gyoza-kun

24:04.960 --> 24:08.850
Every generation is faced with
this question. What is talent?

24:08.850 --> 24:11.620
1% inspiration and 99% sweat?

24:11.620 --> 24:14.090
Effort, effort, effort and more effort?

24:14.090 --> 24:17.530
At the end, there is light.

24:18.440 --> 24:20.320
I'm tired of your pretense.

24:20.320 --> 24:22.390
Talent is success without reason.

24:22.390 --> 24:23.650
Results without reason.

24:23.650 --> 24:26.150
Not even God can make
something out of nothing.

24:26.150 --> 24:29.000
